            "author": {
              "__typename": "User",
              "login": "hclsys"
            },
            "body": "Rebuilt on current main — the branch was 1749 commits behind, so I hand-applied the two hunks rather than resolving a merge, and appended the test to main's current file. Scope is unchanged at +17/-0 with no deletions.\n\nChecked the bug is still live before doing it, rather than rescuing on autopilot. `context.py:454` on main is still `\"code\": args[\"code\"]` with nothing in front of it, so a code_interpreter call whose JSON omits `code` still raises `KeyError` and surfaces as a 500.\n\nRED/GREEN both ways:\n\n```\nsrc reverted, test kept   ->  1 failed,  KeyError: 'code' at context.py:454\nwith the guard            ->  1 passed\nwhole file                ->  17 passed\nruff 0.14.0 (the pin)     ->  check + format clean\nDCO                       ->  signed\n```\n\n`asyncio` wasn't imported in main's version of the test file, so that import is part of the 13 test lines.\n",
